Structural iOS blocker found by the naturalPaint iOS spike (docs/ios-spike-plan.md
Phase 1): upstream OpenColorIO 2.5.2 gates its ICC-profile "which monitor is the
user looking at" helper on bare __APPLE__, which is also true on iOS/tvOS, and
unconditionally includes ColorSync/IOGraphicsLib headers that only exist on macOS.
This is display-color-management UI code, unrelated to headless image I/O, so on
iOS it now falls back to the same empty monitor list already used on Linux
(SystemMonitorsImpl::getAllMonitors() no-op), rather than being ported.


--- a/src/OpenColorIO/SystemMonitor.cpp
+++ b/src/OpenColorIO/SystemMonitor.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,10 @@
 // Copyright Contributors to the OpenColorIO Project.
 
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+#include <TargetConditionals.h>
+#endif
+
 #include <sstream>
 #include <string>
 #include <string.h>
@@ -26,7 +30,7 @@
 
 } // namespace OCIO_NAMESPACE
 
-#elif __APPLE__
+#elif defined(__APPLE__) && TARGET_OS_OSX
 
 #include "SystemMonitor_macos.cpp"
 
